   "source": [
    "# Quiz: Working with Data: Non-Relational Data\n",
    "\n",
    "> **On Alps:** These are the questions of this lesson's pre-lecture and post-lecture quizzes, from the course's quiz app, with the answers the quiz app accepts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pre-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-06-pre-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Spreadsheets are non-relational data</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>True</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Spreadsheets are a kind of non-relational data, along with NoSQL.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>False</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Spreadsheets are a kind of non-relational data, along with NoSQL.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-06-pre-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Identify the difference between non-relational and relational data?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Relational databases always contain columns and rows</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Relational data is organized in columns and rows. Some non-relational data, like graph data, uses nodes and edges instead.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Some types of non-relational data use columns</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. This is true, since columnar stores use columns, but it is not a difference. Relational data uses columns too.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>There is no difference</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. There is a difference. Some non-relational data, like graph data, uses nodes and edges instead of rows.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-06-pre-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What does NoSQL stand for?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Nope SQL</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. One meaning of NoSQL is \"not only SQL.\"</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Not Only SQL</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. NoSQL can mean \"not only SQL.\" Cosmos DB, for example, stores documents but still uses SQL for queries.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>No more SQL</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. NoSQL can mean \"not only SQL.\" Some NoSQL databases, like Cosmos DB, still use SQL.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Post-lecture quiz"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-06-post-1\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>Which one of these is NOT a type of NoSQL?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Object oriented</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. The four NoSQL types are key-value, graph, columnar and document. Object oriented is not one of them.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Key-value</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Key-value is a NoSQL type. It pairs unique keys with values.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Columnar</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Columnar is a NoSQL type. It divides columns into groups called column families.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-06-post-2\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What do you use to do calculations in spreadsheets?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Python</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. In a spreadsheet, you calculate with formulas, which start with an equals sign.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Aliases</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Spreadsheets use formulas to calculate values from cell data.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Formulas</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Formulas perform actions on cell data, like multiplying quantity by cost.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "raw",
   "metadata": {
    "format": "application/vnd.pretext+xml"
   },
   "source": [
    "<exercise label=\"dsb-quiz-06-post-3\">\n",
    "  <statement>\n",
    "    <p>What other type of non-relational data does a document in a document database resemble?</p>\n",
    "  </statement>\n",
    "  <choices randomize=\"no\">\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Keys</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. Documents build on key-value ideas, but a whole document looks like JSON.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice>\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>Column</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Not quite. A document is a set of fields and values, which looks like JSON, not a column.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "    <choice correct=\"yes\">\n",
    "      <statement>\n",
    "        <p>JSON</p>\n",
    "      </statement>\n",
    "      <feedback>\n",
    "        <p>Correct. Documents in a document database look similar to JSON.</p>\n",
    "      </feedback>\n",
    "    </choice>\n",
    "  </choices>\n",
    "</exercise>"
   ]
  }
